# =============================================================================
# Tosh Fair Launchpad -- Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env to git.  .gitignore already excludes it.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployer wallet
# Robinhood Chain uses native ETH for gas, bridged in over the canonical
# Arbitrum bridge or a partner route. There is no faucet-style shortcut on
# mainnet; testnet ETH comes from the Robinhood developer docs.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIVATE_KEY=0xYOUR_PRIVATE_KEY_HERE

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RPC endpoints
#
# ROBINHOOD_RPC is the production target (chain 4663) and ROBINHOOD_TESTNET_RPC
# (46630) is where rehearsals run. Production is chain 4663.
#
# The public endpoints below are rate-limited and carry no archive guarantee or
# SLA. They are fine for a deploy and for wallet traffic; point indexers and
# anything log-heavy at a dedicated provider.
#
# ROBINHOOD_RPC does double duty: it is also what the fork suite
# (test/ToshV5Fork.t.sol) reads for its live-V4 assertions. Unset, those tests
# report SKIPPED rather than failing, so check the log before reading a green
# run as evidence they ran.
#
# No archive capability is needed, and none is available -- state older than a
# few thousand blocks comes back "metadata is not found", which at 100 ms blocks
# is under seventeen minutes of history. That is why the fork suite is unpinned.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROBINHOOD_RPC=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
ROBINHOOD_TESTNET_RPC=https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chain the deploy is ALLOWED to land on. Required by DeployMainnet.s.sol.
#
# This is not a duplicate of the RPC: it is the cross-check ON the RPC. Every
# other address below comes from this file, so a stale or mistyped --rpc-url
# would otherwise deploy a real, ownable, fee-taking factory onto the wrong
# chain, wired to that chain's non-existent V4 PoolManager. The script compares
# `block.chainid` against this and refuses to broadcast on a mismatch.
#
# Set it to the chain you mean, and change it in the same edit as the RPC:
#   4663   Robinhood Chain -- production
#   46630  Robinhood Chain testnet -- staging rehearsals
#
# Note the failure mode if you leave it out. `vm.envUint` reverts on a missing
# variable BEFORE the friendly `require(targetChainId != 0)` can run, so the
# operator sees a Foundry env error rather than "TARGET_CHAIN_ID unset".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TARGET_CHAIN_ID=4663

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contract verification
#
# There is no key to set. Robinhood Chain is served by Blockscout, which does
# not use API keys, and neither Etherscan v2's multichain host nor Basescan
# covers chain 4663 -- so ETHERSCAN_API_KEY and BASESCAN_API_KEY have been
# removed rather than left here to be filled in pointlessly.
#
# Pass `--verifier blockscout` on the forge command line; the URL comes from
# [etherscan] in foundry.toml. Full invocation is in the deploy script headers.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uniswap V4 PoolManager for the network you are deploying to.
# Official list: https://docs.uniswap.org/contracts/v4/deployments
#
# Uniswap deployed V4 on Robinhood Chain themselves, and mainnet and testnet
# share the address -- so a rehearsal exercises the production address book
# unchanged, and this value does not move between the two:
#
#   Robinhood Chain (4663 and 46630)  0x8366a39CC670B4001A1121B8F6A443A643e40951
#
# Get this wrong and every hook is CREATE2'd to an address the PoolManager will
# not accept, with no error until the first launch attempt fails.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
INFINITY_CL_POOL_MANAGER=0x8366a39CC670B4001A1121B8F6A443A643e40951

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PoG oracle signer
# This address's private key is used by the backend to sign PoG gas attestations.
# On testnet: set to your deployer address so you can sign manually with cast.
# On mainnet: use a dedicated hot-wallet address (key lives on the backend server).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POG_SIGNER_ADDRESS=0xYOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform treasury -- ON A MONEY PATH.  REQUIRED, AND UNROTATABLE.
#
# This used to say "legacy, receives nothing", and for one release it was true.
# It is not any more: this address receives 0.30 % of the ETH input of EVERY
# buy, on every pool (ToshLaunchpadHook.PLATFORM_SWAP_FEE_BPS, carved out of
# the 1.00 % swap tax; the other 0.70 % still goes to the buyback reservoir).
# It is the platform's only revenue that is not committed to buyback-and-burn.
#
# There is NO DEFAULT any more.  The deploy scripts used to fall back to the
# deployer address, which was harmless while nothing was paid here and is not
# harmless now -- a forgotten env var would quietly pay the broadcasting key.
#
# IMMUTABLE.  `setPlatformTreasury` was deleted (audit finding M-2: a mutable
# fee-routing target lets the factory owner retarget live fee flows).  The same
# address is also baked into the hook implementation as `platformFeeRecipient`
# at construction.  Choose it BEFORE deploying: changing it means deploying a
# new factory.  A Safe is the right answer.
#
# IT MUST ACCEPT ETH UNCONDITIONALLY.  `poolManager.take` performs a raw value
# transfer and this path is NOT fault-isolated, so a recipient whose receive()
# can revert bricks every buy on every pool.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLATFORM_TREASURY=0xYOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS

# Production owner Safe — MUST differ from the deployer EOA.
# DeployMainnet.s.sol queues Ownable2Step handover to this address.
PROD_OWNER_SAFE=0xYOUR_GNOSIS_SAFE

# =============================================================================
# Post-deployment: fill these in after running forge script
# =============================================================================
FACTORY_ADDRESS=0x
LADDER_TREASURY_ADDRESS=0x
